<!-- Subtitle chooser: a self-contained, FULL-SCREEN WindowXMLDialog, the same on every skin (Estuary, Arctic
     Fuse 3, ...). Only the universal font12 / font13 / font14 names and the textures bundled in this add-on
     skin's media are used.

     ROWS. One column per field, each column holds text of ONE direction (a Latin release name, a Latin
     provider, a Hebrew chip), so Kodi's bidirectional layout can never reorder the pieces of a row:
       flag | match % + its Hebrew tier word | release filename (line 1) ; provider + up to 3 chips (line 2)
     INFO PANEL. Reads the FOCUSED row (Container(100).ListItem.Property(...)), so it follows the list by
     itself, with no Python on a focus change: the full release name, the breakdown of why it matched (episode,
     edition, frame rate, source, group, streaming service, proven timing), and the provider / type / language /
     accessibility of the subtitle. Rows and properties are built in ui/chooser_rows.py; the colours are baked
     into the property text (BBCode), a per-row <textcolor>$INFO[...]</textcolor> is unreliable in Kodi.
     PROVENANCE (Hebrew provider rows): a badge chip in the row's chips and, in the right panel between the release name and the
     match rows, the "איכות ומקור הכתובית" block with the provider's own metadata and the credits read inside the downloaded file
     (p_prov, p_prov_src, p_translator, p_sync, p_uploader, p_date, p_downloads, p_fixed; has_meta shows / hides the block).
     Positive only: a row without evidence has no badge and no "unverified" text.
     Ids: list 100, manual search 202, back to the automatic list 203 (only while a manual result is shown: window
     property subs.manual), cancel translation 204, subtitle settings 205, cancel the automatic sync 206 (only while
     the current subtitle was synced automatically: window property subs.sync.mode), close 201. Button row (left to
     right): 205 204 203 206 | 202 201; every button goes up to the list, left / right walk the row (a hidden 203 / 206
     is skipped). AUTO-SYNC BADGE (header): "סונכרנה אוטומטית" + the applied shift, read from the Home window
     properties subs.sync.offset ('+2.5s', '-1.2s', 'מקטעים', 'שינוי קצב') and subs.sync.mode (core/selection.py);
     the value is its own control so a Latin number never mixes with the Hebrew words (bidi).
     Manual search (ui/chooser.py, ui/manual_prompts.py, fetching/manual.py) asks for a title and a year, or a show, a
     season and an episode, and shows the rows here; "חזרה לרשימה" brings the automatic list back. The window name stays script.moransubs.chooser.xml and the
     property MoranSubsChooserOpen is set by ui/chooser.py (both read by skins). -->
